def build_core(p,add):
 add('preliminaries','DFT、卷积与符号作用域','DFT, convolution and notation scopes','Section3 Eqs1–2',r'G_{uv}^{(c)}=\sum_{m,n}F_{mn}^{(c)}e^{-2\pi i(um/M+vn/N)}',[3],[GRID],[DFT,CAS],[st('区分空间与谱','Separate spatial and spectral objects',r'原$F,W,b$是实空间数组，$G,H,T$是复频谱。原$g^{(uv)}$是输入通道DFT列向量，并非coalition game $g_x(S)=v(x_S)$；不中心化或默认偏置0。',r'The source $F,W,b$ are real spatial arrays and $G,H,T$ are complex spectra. The source $g^{(uv)}$ is the input-channel DFT column, distinct from the coalition game $g_x(S)=v(x_S)$. It is not centered and biases are not set to zero.')],('定义入口；正交、传播和矩推导有各自目标。','A definition entry; orthogonality, propagation and moments have separate targets.'),keys=['main-preliminaries'],kind='definition',role='source_material',symbols=['grid','input-feature','input-spectrum','kernel','kernel-response','bias'])
 add('assumption-3-1','保持尺寸的卷积模型','The size-preserving convolution model','Assumption3.1',r'\mathrm{stride}=1,\quad\mathrm{padding}=\mathrm{circular}',[3],[LINEAR],[GRID,DFT],[st('固定原模型','Fix the source model',r'circular padding把索引加法放在有限循环网格；核偏移仍取原有限索引。zero padding和stride变化不自动属于本精确传播模型。',r'Circular padding puts index addition on the finite cyclic grid; kernel offsets retain their original finite indices. Zero padding and changed strides are not automatically part of this exact model.')],('原假设入口；与实验网络范围分开。','An entry for the source assumption, separate from experimental-network scope.'),keys=['main-assumption-3.1','main-linear-network-setting'],kind='assumption',role='source_material',symbols=['grid','kernel','depth','channels'])
 add('geometric-sum','Lemma A.1：有限和与零分母','Lemma A.1: finite sums and zero denominators','LemmaA.1 Eqs13–14',r'\sum_{t<n}e^{it\theta}=\frac{\sin(n\theta/2)}{\sin(\theta/2)}e^{i(n-1)\theta/2}',[11,12],[('原量词为任意实θ与正整数n，保留这个全称范围。','The source quantifies over arbitrary real θ and positive integers n; retain this universal scope.')],[FINITE],[st('从有限和开始','Start from the finite sum',r'令$z=e^{i\theta}$。逐项相减得$(1-z)P_n(z)=1-z^n$；$z=1$时和直接为$n$，这给全域合法定义。',r'Let $z=e^{i\theta}$. Telescoping gives $(1-z)P_n(z)=1-z^n$. At $z=1$, the finite sum directly equals $n$, giving an everywhere-defined expression.',r'(1-z)P_n(z)=1-z^n',names('geometric_telescoping','geometric_one')),st('核对商的合法域','Check the quotient domain',r'$z\ne1$时除以$1-z$，用$1-e^{it\theta}=-2ie^{it\theta/2}\sin(t\theta/2)$得作者商。$\theta\in2\pi\mathbb Z$时普通实商未定义，有限和及极限仍为$n$，不能声称原全称商定义式成立。',r'For $z\ne1$, divide by $1-z$ and use $1-e^{it\theta}=-2ie^{it\theta/2}\sin(t\theta/2)$ to obtain the source quotient. At $\theta\in2\pi\mathbb Z$, the ordinary quotient is undefined, although the finite sum and limiting value are $n$.',r'P_n(1)=n',names('geometric_quotient'))],('有限和、望远镜和非单位根复商已形式化；实三角商证明与原定义域问题分开。','The finite sum, telescoping and non-unit complex quotient are formalized; the human trigonometric proof is separate from the original domain issue.'),keys=['lemma-A.1'],role='partial_proof_with_refuted_clause',assessment='partially_refuted',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['geometric','phase-sum','kernel-size'])
 add('orthogonality','二维字符正交与逆DFT','Two-dimensional character orthogonality and inverse DFT','Eqs15–16; A.3 Eq19',r'\sum_{m,n}\chi_{uv}(m,n)\overline{\chi_{u^{\prime}v^{\prime}}(m,n)}=MN\delta_{uu^{\prime}}\delta_{vv^{\prime}}',[12,15],[GRID],[DFT],[st('分离坐标字符','Separate coordinate characters',r'二维指数是两个循环字符的乘积。非平凡字符经一个字符值非1的平移迫使总和0；平凡字符逐项1，和为$M$或$N$。乘两坐标结果得二维正交。',r'The two-dimensional exponential is a product of cyclic characters. Translating a nontrivial character by an element with value different from one forces its sum to zero. A trivial character sums to $M$ or $N$. Multiplying the two results gives orthogonality.',r'\sum_{m,n}\chi_{uv}\overline{\chi_{u^{\prime}v^{\prime}}}=MN\delta_{uu^{\prime}}\delta_{vv^{\prime}}',names('grid_orthogonality','grid_character_sum')),st('消去逆变换频率和','Eliminate the inverse-transform frequency sum',r'把DFT代入逆式，交换有限和，正交只保留原位置，$MN$与逆式$(MN)^{-1}$抵消。对任意复输入两个方向均成立。',r'Substitute the DFT into its inverse, exchange finite sums, and use orthogonality to retain only the original position. The factor MN cancels $(MN)^{-1}$. Both directions hold for arbitrary complex inputs.',r'f_{mn}=\frac1{MN}\sum_{u,v}\widehat f_{uv}e^{2\pi i(um/M+vn/N)}',names('inverse_dft2','dft2_inverse'))],('实际二维循环网格的正交和双向逆DFT完整验证。','Orthogonality and both inverse-DFT directions on the actual two-dimensional cyclic grid are fully verified.'),keys=['orthogonality'],symbols=['grid','input-spectrum','inverse-dft','delta'])
 add('forward-convolution','Theorem 3.2：实际卷积到DFT','Theorem 3.2: actual convolution to the DFT','Theorem3.2 Eq3; A.1 Eq18',r'h^{(uv)}=T^{(uv)}g^{(uv)}+\delta_{uv}MN b',[3,12,13,14],[LINEAR],[GRID,DFT,CAS],[st('变换真实正偏移','Transform the actual positive shift',r'原算子取$f_c(x+t)$。令$y=x+t$重编号，负输出相位产生正因子$\chi_{uv}(t)$，所以$\widehat{f_c(\cdot+t)}=\chi_{uv}(t)\widehat f_c$。',r'The source operator uses $f_c(x+t)$. Reindex by $y=x+t$: the negative output phase gives the positive factor $\chi_{uv}(t)$, so $\widehat{f_c(\cdot+t)}=\chi_{uv}(t)\widehat f_c$.',r'\widehat{f_c(\cdot+t)}=\chi_{uv}(t)\widehat f_c',names('offset_layer_dft')),st('收集核与通道系数','Collect kernel and channel coefficients',r'交换有限偏移、通道和网格求和，收集成$T_{dc}^{(uv)}$。不同核位置若循环后重合，按原核和仍计两项，证明不加偏移injective假设。',r'Exchange the finite offset, channel and grid sums and collect $T_{dc}^{(uv)}$. Distinct kernel positions that coincide modulo the grid still contribute separately; no injective-offset assumption is added.',r'T_{dc}^{(uv)}=\sum_{t,s}W_{cts}^{[\mathrm{ker}=d]}\chi_{uv}(t,s)',names('square_kernel_response')),st('保留DC偏置','Retain DC bias',r'常数$b_d$的DFT在DC为$MN b_d$，非DC为0。由此得到完整原矩阵式；A.1末行下标复用在项目证明重编号修复，不改命题。',r'The DFT of constant $b_d$ is $MN b_d$ at DC and zero elsewhere, giving the complete source matrix formula. The reused indices in the last line of A.1 are repaired by reindexing the proof, without changing the theorem.',r'\widehat b(u,v)=MN\delta_{uv}b',names('dft2_constant'))],('实际多通道空间卷积、原相位和MN偏置全部验证。','The actual multichannel spatial convolution, original phases and MN bias are fully verified.'),keys=['A.1'],symbols=['grid','input-feature','input-spectrum','kernel','kernel-response','bias','delta','channels'])
 valid=source('A.1')['original_proof_md']
 a17=valid[valid.find('When'):valid.find('When')] if False else ''
 add('valid-convolution','无padding的跨频混合与Eq17错式','Valid-convolution mixing and the Equation (17) error','A.1 Eq17',r'\alpha_{u^{\prime}v^{\prime}uv}=\frac1{MN}\sum_{m=0}^{M-K}\sum_{n=0}^{N-K}e^{2\pi i(\lambda m+\gamma n)}',[13],[('无padding、stride1，1≤K≤min(M,N)，M′=M−K+1、N′=N−K+1。','Valid convolution uses stride one, 1≤K≤min(M,N), M′=M−K+1 and N′=N−K+1.')],[DFT,FINITE],[st('核对有限和项数','Check the finite-sum count',r'输入逆DFT代入空间卷积，输出在$M^{\prime}\times N^{\prime}$网格上变换得有限$\alpha$。每个坐标分别有$M-K+1$与$N-K+1$项，而原商写$M-K$与$N-K$。',r'Substitute the inverse DFT into convolution and transform the output on the $M^{\prime}\times N^{\prime}$ grid. Each coordinate sum has $M-K+1$ or $N-K+1$ terms, whereas the printed quotient uses $M-K$ or $N-K$.'),st('使用非零分母反例','Use a counterexample with nonzero denominators',r'取$M=N=3,K=2,u=v=0,u^{\prime}=v^{\prime}=1$，则$\lambda=\gamma=-1/2$。正确和$(1+e^{-i\pi})^2/9=0$，原商两个比值为1、相位为$e^{-i\pi}=-1$，所以原右式$-1/9$。这不依赖零分母。',r'For $M=N=3,K=2,u=v=0,u^{\prime}=v^{\prime}=1$, both λ and γ equal −1/2. The correct sum is $(1+e^{-i\pi})^2/9=0$; the two printed ratios equal one and the phase is $e^{-i\pi}=-1$, giving $-1/9$. This does not rely on zero denominators.',r'\alpha_{\rm finite}=0\ne-\frac19=\alpha_{\rm printed}')],('精确人读反例；该非循环具体反例尚未单独形式化，未冒充机器反例。','An exact human counterexample; this concrete non-circular case has not yet been separately formalized and is not presented as machine evidence.'),original=r'In the scenario of no padding, $$M^{\prime}=M-K+1,\quad N^{\prime}=N-K+1.$$ $$\alpha_{u^{\prime}v^{\prime}uv}=\frac1{MN}\sum_{m=0}^{M-K}e^{2\pi i\lambda_{uu^{\prime}}m}\sum_{n=0}^{N-K}e^{2\pi i\gamma_{vv^{\prime}}n}=\frac1{MN}\frac{\sin((M-K)\lambda_{uu^{\prime}}\pi)}{\sin(\lambda_{uu^{\prime}}\pi)}\frac{\sin((N-K)\gamma_{vv^{\prime}}\pi)}{\sin(\gamma_{vv^{\prime}}\pi)}e^{i((M-K)\lambda_{uu^{\prime}}+(N-K)\gamma_{vv^{\prime}})\pi}.\tag{17}$$',proof='',role='counterexample',assessment='counterexample_recorded',leanrole='none',symbols=['grid','valid-mixing','geometric'])
 add('cascade-forward','Corollary 3.3：层积与完整偏置','Corollary 3.3: layer products and complete bias','Corollary3.3 Eq4; A.2',r'h^{(uv)}=\mathbb T^{(uv)(L:1)}g^{(uv)}+\delta_{uv}\beta',[4,14],[LINEAR],[DFT,CAS],[st('归纳有序层积','Induct over ordered layer products',r'逐层$g_l=T_lg_{l-1}+\delta MNb_l$。若前缀线性项为$A_{l-1}$，下一层为$T_lA_{l-1}$，相容线性映射允许不同通道宽度，不能交换层次。',r'Each layer gives $g_l=T_lg_{l-1}+\delta MNb_l$. A prefix linear part $A_{l-1}$ becomes $T_lA_{l-1}$. Compatible maps allow different widths; layers cannot be exchanged.',r'A_l=T_lA_{l-1}',names('actual_grid_cascade')),st('展开所有偏置','Expand all biases',r'$c_l=T_lc_{l-1}+\delta MNb_l$归纳得$\delta MN[b_L+\sum_{j=2}^L\mathbb T^{(00)(L:j)}b_{j-1}]$。正文MN乘全括号正确；A.2一行额外内层MN及层上标误用是局部证明笔误。',r'Inducting on $c_l=T_lc_{l-1}+\delta MNb_l$ yields $\delta MN[b_L+\sum_{j=2}^L\mathbb T^{(00)(L:j)}b_{j-1}]$. The main formula correctly multiplies the whole bracket by MN. An extra inner MN and reused layer superscripts in A.2 are local proof slips.',r'\beta=MN\left[b_L+\sum_{j=2}^L\mathbb T^{(00)(L:j)}b_{j-1}\right]',names('cascade_bias_sum'))],('真实有限深度、变化通道宽度、有序层积及全部偏置完整验证。','Actual finite depth, varying widths, ordered products and all biases are fully verified.'),keys=['main-corollary-3.3','A.2'],symbols=['grid','input-spectrum','kernel-response','cascade-response','bias','depth','channels','delta'])
 mainback=source('main-corollary-3.4')['original_statement_md']
 add('backpropagation','Corollary 3.4：实梯度与频域pullback','Corollary 3.4: real gradients and spectral pullbacks','Corollary3.4 Eq5; A.3 Eqs19–26',mainback.split('$$')[1].split(r'\tag')[0],[4,15,16,17,18],[LINEAR,('Loss对真实实feature与权重可微；更新W−η∇W Loss，保留共轭频率约束。','The loss is differentiable in actual real features and weights; update W−η∇W Loss, retaining conjugate-frequency constraints.')],[DFT,CAS,FINITE],[st('求真实实权重导数','Differentiate actual real weights',r'单层核到输出feature是实连续线性映射。上层loss导数实泛函$J$的基分解给$r_{dcts}=\sum_{m,n}F_c(m+t,n+s)D_d(m,n)$，$D_d$是其Riesz坐标；不是独立复T的形式偏导。',r'The map from a layer’s kernel to its output is real continuous linear. Basis decomposition of the upper real loss functional J gives $r_{dcts}=\sum_{m,n}F_c(m+t,n+s)D_d(m,n)$, with D its Riesz coordinates, rather than a formal derivative in unconstrained complex T.',r'r_{dcts}=\sum_{m,n}F_c(m+t,n+s)D_d(m,n)',names('actual_real_layer_loss_hasFDerivAt','actual_real_kernel_pullback')),st('用Parseval传送梯度','Transport the gradient using Parseval',r'实际位移内积为$(MN)^{-1}\sum_k\overline{\chi_k(t)\widehat F_c(k)}\widehat D_d(k)$。再按核偏移求正相位和，得到$\sum_k\chi_{k,uv}\overline{\widehat F_c(k)}\widehat D_d(k)$。有限χ包含所有对角项。',r'The actual shifted inner product is $(MN)^{-1}\sum_k\overline{\chi_k(t)\widehat F_c(k)}\widehat D_d(k)$. Summing positive phases over kernel offsets yields $\sum_k\chi_{k,uv}\overline{\widehat F_c(k)}\widehat D_d(k)$. The finite χ includes every diagonal term.',r'q_{dc}(u,v)=\sum_k\chi_{k,uv}\overline{\widehat F_c(k)}\widehat D_d(k)',names('spectral_kernel_pullback','actual_real_spatial_pullback','cross_frequency_diagonal')),st('更新并区分复导数约定','Update and distinguish complex derivative conventions',r'$T$对实W线性，精确$\Delta T=-\eta\sum r_{ts}\chi_{uv}(t,s)=-\eta MNq$。标准实Riesz梯度为$2\partial_{\bar z}Loss$，原复偏导等同实偏导需说明其约定。前缀用Cor3.3，后缀泛函经共轭谱矩阵传递；当前机器尚未独立组合整条前后缀显式矩阵链。',r'Linearity in real W gives the exact $\Delta T=-\eta\sum r_{ts}\chi_{uv}(t,s)=-\eta MNq$. The standard real Riesz gradient is $2\partial_{\bar z}Loss$, so the source identification with a real derivative needs its convention stated. Corollary 3.3 supplies the prefix; the suffix functional passes through conjugate spectral matrices. The entire explicit prefix/suffix chain has not yet been separately composed in Lean.',r'\Delta T=-\eta MNq',names('actual_response_gradient_update'))],('已验证真实单层实Fréchet导数、空间核坐标、Parseval χ和精确更新；原Eq5整条显式前后缀矩阵链待组合，任意J不冒充该整目标。','Actual single-layer real Fréchet derivatives, kernel coordinates, Parseval χ and exact updates are verified. The explicit full prefix/suffix chain in Equation (5) still needs composition; an arbitrary J is not presented as that whole target.'),keys=['main-corollary-3.4','A.3'],role='partial_component',assessment='partially_refuted',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['grid','input-spectrum','kernel-response','cascade-response','cross-frequency','loss','learning-rate','gradient'])

def build_moments(p,add):
 a4=source('A.4')['original_proof_md']
 assumption,body=a4.split('Then, we prove Theorem 4.2, as follows.',1)
 gaussian,single=body.split('**Then, we prove Theorem 4.2 as follows.**',1)
 single,multi=single.split('**For the more general case',1)
 multi='**For the more general case'+multi
 add('independence-scope','Assumption 4.1：独立与一阶矩分解','Assumption 4.1: independence versus first-moment factorization','Assumption4.1 Eqs6–7; A.4 initial argument',r'\mathbb E[T_lT_{l^{\prime}}]=\mathbb ET_l\,\mathbb ET_{l^{\prime}}',[5,18,19],[('原显示Eq6只对d≠d′且c≠c′；Eq7对不同层只写一阶乘积均值。原英文irrelevant及其初始化解释保留，独立读取和弱显示式读取分别评估。','Displayed Equation (6) requires both d≠d′ and c≠c′, while (7) only states first-product expectations between layers. Retain the word irrelevant and its initialization argument; assess genuine independence separately from the weak displayed equations.')],[SOM,GAUSS],[
 st('解释实际初始化的独立性','Interpret independence of actual initialization',r'若各核/层由独立Gaussian数组初始化，不同层的$T_l$是不同独立数组的可测函数，因此独立；这个模型足以推出平方模矩乘积分解。少数参数被更新的lottery-ticket引用并不自动保持独立，训练后须重新核对概率模型。',r'With independently initialized Gaussian arrays, each $T_l$ is a measurable function of a distinct independent weight vector, hence the responses are independent. This model yields squared-magnitude product moments. The lottery-ticket citation about a few updated parameters does not by itself preserve independence after training.',r'SOM(\prod_lT_l)=\prod_lSOM(T_l)',names('actual_independent_layer_moments')),
 st('核对显示等式的不足','Check the insufficiency of the displays',r'只读Eq6–7时，取$K=1,L=2$、单通道，$U\sim\mathcal N(0,1)$，独立均匀符号$B\in\{-1,1\}$，$W_1=U,W_2=BU$。两层边缘均标准Gaussian，$\mathbb E[W_1W_2]=\mathbb E[B]\mathbb E[U^2]=0$满足Eq7，Eq6单通道无实例；但$\mathbb E|W_1W_2|^2=\mathbb EU^4=3\ne1$。这是弱显示条件不足，不否定真正独立模型。',r'Under Equations (6)–(7) alone, take K=1, L=2 and one channel. Let U be standard Gaussian and B an independent uniform sign, with $W_1=U,W_2=BU$. Both marginals are standard Gaussian and $\mathbb E[W_1W_2]=\mathbb E[B]\mathbb E[U^2]=0$ satisfies (7); (6) is vacuous. However, $\mathbb E|W_1W_2|^2=\mathbb EU^4=3\ne1$. This demonstrates insufficiency of the weak displays, without refuting genuine independence.',r'\mathbb E|U\cdot BU|^2=3\ne1')],
 ('独立模型的真实矩证明已编译；U/BU对弱显示条件的反例目前为完整人读计算，未声称该随机构造已Lean编码。','The actual independent-model moment proof is compiled. The U/BU construction is currently a complete human counterexample to the weak displays, without claiming that random construction is encoded in Lean.'),keys=['main-assumption-4.1'],proof=assumption,proofpages=[18,19],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['kernel','kernel-response','mean','variance','som','independence'])
 add('gaussian-response','真实实Gaussian核的复响应与伪协方差','Complex responses and pseudocovariance of real Gaussian kernels','A.4 Eq27',r'\mathbb ET=\mu_lR_{uv},\quad V(T)=K^2\sigma_l^2,\quad C(T)=\sigma_l^2R_{2u,2v}',[19,20],[GAUSS],[DFT,FINITE,SOM],[
 st('从实Gaussian嵌入开始','Start with embedded real Gaussians',r'设$W_t$独立实Gaussian。每个$e^{i\theta_t}W_t$是实Gaussian律经连续实线性映射进入$\mathbb C$；有限独立和仍为实二维Gaussian。不能把实$W$误当圆对称复Gaussian：$\mathbb E(W-\mu)^2=\sigma^2$而非0。',r'Each independent real Gaussian weight $W_t$ maps into $\mathbb C$ by the continuous real linear map $w\mapsto e^{i\theta_t}w$. A finite independent sum remains a real two-dimensional Gaussian. A real W is not a circular complex Gaussian: $\mathbb E(W-\mu)^2=\sigma^2$, rather than zero.',r'C(W)=\sigma^2',names('gaussian_weighted_isGaussian','real_gaussian_pseudocovariance','actual_kernel_gaussian')),
 st('计算均值与平方模矩','Compute the mean and squared-magnitude moment',r'可积有限和给$\mathbb ET=\sum_t\mu e^{i\theta_t}=\mu R$。中心化双和中，不同独立核元素项期望0，单位相位对角项为$\sigma^2$，故$V(T)=K^2\sigma^2$，$SOM(T)=|\mu R|^2+K^2\sigma^2$。Gaussian真实律提供L²可积性。',r'Integrability of the finite sum gives $\mathbb ET=\mu R$. In its centered double sum, distinct independent weights have zero cross expectation, while diagonal unit phases contribute $\sigma^2$. Thus $V(T)=K^2\sigma^2$ and $SOM(T)=|\mu R|^2+K^2\sigma^2$. Actual Gaussian laws supply L² integrability.',r'SOM(T)=|\mu R|^2+K^2\sigma^2',names('actual_kernel_mean','actual_kernel_second_moment','weighted_response_centered_square')),
 st('保留伪协方差相位平方','Retain squared phases in pseudocovariance',r'不取共轭的中心化平方，仍只剩对角项，但相位平方为$e^{2i\theta_t}$，所以$C(T)=\sigma^2R_{2u,2v}$。这是原Eq27正确结果；A.4先写实权重的复伪协方差0的步骤错误由正确实嵌入证明修复。',r'Without conjugation, only diagonal centered terms remain, but each phase becomes $e^{2i\theta_t}$, giving $C(T)=\sigma^2R_{2u,2v}$. This is the correct result in Equation (27). The earlier A.4 claim of zero pseudocovariance for real weights is repaired using the actual real embedding.',r'C(T)=\sigma^2R_{2u,2v}',names('actual_kernel_pseudocovariance'))],
 ('真正独立实Gaussian核的复Gaussian闭包、实际积分均值/二阶矩/伪协方差已验证；依赖独立prose读取，不仅边缘Gaussian加不相关。R全域以原有限和解释。','Complex Gaussian closure and actual mean, second-moment and pseudocovariance integrals are verified for genuinely independent real Gaussian weights. This uses the independence reading of the prose, rather than merely Gaussian marginals and uncorrelatedness. R is interpreted everywhere by its source finite sum.'),original=source('A.4')['original_statement_md'],proof=gaussian,proofpages=[19,20],symbols=['kernel','kernel-response','phase-sum','mean','variance','pseudocovariance','som','independence'])
 add('single-channel-moments','Theorem 4.2：单通道实际乘积矩与log','Theorem 4.2: actual single-channel product moments and logs','Theorem4.2; A.4 Eq28 and unnumbered product proof',r'SOM(\mathbb T^{(uv)(L:1)})=\prod_{l=1}^L(|\mu_lR_{uv}|^2+K^2\sigma_l^2)',[5,20,21],[GAUSS,('原单通道C_l=1；普通log公式适用于每个矩因子正的域。标准非退化Gaussianσ_l²>0和K>0保证这一点，退化零方差另说明。','The source assumes C_l=1. The ordinary logarithm formula applies where every moment factor is positive. Standard nondegenerate Gaussian variances σ_l²>0 and K>0 ensure this; degenerate zero-variance cases are explained separately.')],[DFT,CAS,SOM,FINITE],[
 st('从实际层数组得到响应独立','Derive response independence from actual layer arrays',r'每个$T_l$是该层有限实核数组的可测相位和。整个层向量独立经可测函数保持，得到$T_l$独立，平方模也独立；未假设所求矩等式。',r'Each T_l is a measurable phase sum of its finite real kernel array. Measurable functions of independent layer vectors remain independent, as do their squared magnitudes; the desired moment equality is not assumed.',r'|{\prod_lT_l}|^2=\prod_l|T_l|^2',names('actual_independent_layer_moments')),
 st('积分真实平方模乘积','Integrate the actual squared-magnitude product',r'用公共独立乘积积分定理到实值$|T_l|^2$，得期望乘积为期望之积；代入前一Gaussian核矩，得到原乘积式。空层积为1，有限层结果不依渐近或LLN。',r'Apply the shared independent-product integral theorem to the real variables $|T_l|^2$, then substitute the actual Gaussian kernel moments. The empty layer product is one; the finite-depth result needs neither asymptotics nor the law of large numbers.',r'\mathbb E\prod_l|T_l|^2=\prod_l\mathbb E|T_l|^2',names('independent_complex_product_second_moment')),
 st('在正矩域展开log','Expand logs on the positive-moment domain',r'$|\mu_lR|^2\ge0$且$K^2\sigma_l^2>0$，故各因子和乘积正，普通实log的乘积法则合法。退化因子0时原log未定义；不能用Lean的Real.log0总化值把原log全域命题认作通过。',r'$|\mu_lR|^2\ge0$ and $K^2\sigma_l^2>0$ make every factor and the product positive, permitting the ordinary logarithm product rule. At a degenerate zero factor the source log is undefined; Lean’s totalized Real.log 0 is not used to assert a globally defined source logarithm.',r'\log SOM(\mathbb T)=\sum_l\log(|\mu_lR|^2+K^2\sigma_l^2)',names('actual_independent_layer_log_moments'))],
 ('真正独立层模型的实际单通道乘积SOM及正矩log完整验证；源Eq6–7弱条件与无条件指数增长独立评估。','The actual single-channel SOM product and positive-domain logarithm are fully verified for genuinely independent layers. The weak displayed conditions and unconditional exponential-growth interpretation are assessed separately.'),keys=['main-theorem-4.2'],proof=single,proofpages=[20,21],symbols=['cascade-response','kernel-response','phase-sum','som','mean','variance','depth','independence'])
 add('multi-channel-moments','A.4：多通道均值、SOM递推与附加独立范围','A.4: multichannel means, SOM recurrences and extra independence','A.4 Eqs29–32',r'm_L=C_{L-1}\mu_LR\,m_{L-1},\quad s_L=C_{L-1}a_Ls_{L-1}+C_{L-1}(C_{L-1}-1)|\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}|^2',[21,22],[GAUSS,('原A.4额外说所有级联矩阵元素独立；显示条件仍仅d≠d′且c≠c′的一阶矩。证明递推需要同一列不同中间行的共轭交叉矩，不能由这显示式自动推出。','A.4 additionally says that all cascade-matrix entries are independent. Its display still only covers d≠d′ and c≠c′ first moments. The SOM recurrence needs conjugated cross moments between different intermediate rows in the same column, which the display alone does not provide.')],[SOM,CAS,(r'令$m_l=\mathbb E\mathbb T_{dc}^{(l:1)}$、$s_l=\mathbb E|\mathbb T_{dc}^{(l:1)}|^2$，$a_l=|\mu_lR|^2+K^2\sigma_l^2$。这些是矩阵逐元素均值/矩，不是矩阵乘法的平方。',r'Let $m_l=\mathbb E\mathbb T_{dc}^{(l:1)}$, $s_l=\mathbb E|\mathbb T_{dc}^{(l:1)}|^2$, and $a_l=|\mu_lR|^2+K^2\sigma_l^2$. These are entrywise matrix means and moments, not the square of matrix multiplication.')],[
 st('求各元素及层积均值','Compute entry and cascade means',r'Eq29–30逐元素应用真实单核均值与SOM。对矩阵积$(T_LP)_{dc}=\sum_jT_{dj}P_{jc}$，当前层与旧层独立给$\mathbb E(T_LP)_{dc}=\sum_j\mathbb ET_{dj}\mathbb EP_{jc}$。同质均值时$m_L=C_{L-1}\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}$；有限归纳得$m_L=(\prod_{l<L}C_l)(\prod_{l\le L}\mu_lR)$。',r'Equations (29)–(30) apply the actual kernel mean and SOM entrywise. For $(T_LP)_{dc}=\sum_jT_{dj}P_{jc}$, independence of the current and previous layers gives $\mathbb E(T_LP)_{dc}=\sum_j\mathbb ET_{dj}\mathbb EP_{jc}$. Homogeneous means satisfy $m_L=C_{L-1}\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}$, yielding $m_L=(\prod_{l<L}C_l)(\prod_{l\le L}\mu_lR)$ by finite induction.',r'm_L=C_{L-1}\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}',names('actual_kernel_mean','actual_kernel_second_moment')),
 st('区分对角与共轭交叉项','Separate diagonal and conjugated cross terms',r'展开$\mathbb E|\sum_jT_{dj}P_{jc}|^2$。对角贡献$C_{L-1}a_Ls_{L-1}$；若原额外prose真的提供同列行间独立，各$j\ne k$贡献$|\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}|^2$，共有$C_{L-1}(C_{L-1}-1)$项。仅显示Eq6/额外一阶式不够；一般深层iid网络的P条目共享先前权重，也不能无证自动独立。',r'Expand $\mathbb E|\sum_jT_{dj}P_{jc}|^2$. The diagonal contributes $C_{L-1}a_Ls_{L-1}$. If the extra prose really supplies independence of different rows in the same column, each j≠k term is $|\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}|^2$, with $C_{L-1}(C_{L-1}-1)$ such terms. The weak displays do not suffice, and entries of a deep iid cascade share earlier weights, so their independence cannot be inferred without proof.',r's_L=C_{L-1}a_Ls_{L-1}+C_{L-1}(C_{L-1}-1)|\mu_LR\,m_{L-1}|^2'),
 st('有限展开递推而非无条件增长','Unroll the recurrence without asserting unconditional growth',r'令$b_l=C_{l-1}a_l$、$d_l=C_{l-1}(C_{l-1}-1)|\mu_lR\,m_{l-1}|^2$，则$s_L=s_1\prod_{j=2}^Lb_j+\sum_{l=2}^Ld_l\prod_{j=l+1}^Lb_j$，归纳直接验证。这是Eq32的条件性有限闭式；正数因子可以小于1，不能从它推出普遍指数增加。',r'With $b_l=C_{l-1}a_l$ and $d_l=C_{l-1}(C_{l-1}-1)|\mu_lR\,m_{l-1}|^2$, finite induction gives $s_L=s_1\prod_{j=2}^Lb_j+\sum_{l=2}^Ld_l\prod_{j=l+1}^Lb_j$. This is the conditional finite closed form in (32); positive factors may be below one, so it does not imply universal exponential growth.',r's_L=s_1\prod_{j=2}^Lb_j+\sum_{l=2}^Ld_l\prod_{j=l+1}^Lb_j')],
 ('实际单核均值/SOM已验证；本矩阵均值、必要共轭递推及有限闭式目前人读完整，机器矩阵随机适配仍待补，未称全目标通过。','Actual single-kernel means and SOMs are verified. The matrix mean, required conjugated recurrence and finite closed form currently have complete human proofs; the random-matrix machine adapter remains to be added and is not reported as a whole-target proof.'),original=multi.split('Proof.',1)[0],proof='Proof.'+multi.split('Proof.',1)[1],proofpages=[21,22],role='partial_component',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['cascade-response','channels','som','mean','variance','depth','independence'])
 conclusions=source('main-theorem-4.2-five-conclusions')['original_statement_md']
 chunks={i:conclusions.split(f'({i}) ',1)[1].split(f'({i+1}) ',1)[0] if i<5 else conclusions.split('(5) ',1)[1].split('Experiments in Section',1)[0] for i in range(1,6)}
 add('moment-parameter-growth','推论(1)：参数单调性与K/R耦合','Conclusion (1): parameter monotonicity and coupled K/R','Theorem4.2 interpretation (1)',r'a_l=|\mu_lR_{uv}|^2+K^2\sigma_l^2',[5],[GAUSS],[FINITE,SOM],[
 st('固定其他量检查单调性','Check monotonicity with other quantities fixed',r'$a_l$在固定$K,R$时随$|\mu_l|$、$\sigma_l^2$非减，在固定$|\mu_l|$时随$|R|$非减；可以非严格，例如$\mu_l=0$时R无影响。非负因子乘积保持非减。',r'With K and R fixed, a_l is nondecreasing in $|\mu_l|$ and $\sigma_l^2$, and with $|\mu_l|$ fixed it is nondecreasing in $|R|$. Growth may be non-strict, for example when μ_l=0. Products of nonnegative factors preserve this monotonicity.'),
 st('让K按原核改变R','Let K change R as the actual kernel does',r'$R_{uv}$本身依赖K。取$M=N=8,L=1,\mu=1,\sigma^2=1/16$、频率$(4,0)$：K=1有R=1、SOM=$17/16$；K=2两相位1与−1抵消，R=0、SOM=$1/4$，所以原普遍随K增加的子句失败。',r'R_uv itself depends on K. For M=N=8, L=1, μ=1, σ²=1/16 and frequency (4,0), K=1 gives R=1 and SOM=17/16. At K=2, phases one and minus one cancel, giving R=0 and SOM=1/4. Thus the universal K-growth subclause fails.',r'\frac{17}{16}>\frac14')],
 ('固定量的条件单调性与原K子句反例分开；本数值核/真实Gaussian矩的人读适配尚未独立Lean编码。','Conditional monotonicity with fixed quantities is separated from the K-subclause counterexample. This concrete kernel/Gaussian-moment calculation is not yet independently encoded in Lean.'),original='(1) '+chunks[1],proof='',role='partial_proof_with_refuted_clause',assessment='partially_refuted',leanrole='none',symbols=['phase-sum','kernel-size','mean','variance','som'])
 add('depth-growth','推论(2)：真实Gaussian深度递减反例','Conclusion (2): actual Gaussian depth-decay counterexample','Theorem4.2 interpretation (2)',r'SOM(\mathbb T_L)=(1/4)^L',[5,21,22],[GAUSS,('反例K=1、单通道、每层独立N(0,1/4)，满足原真实独立模型。','The counterexample has K=1, one channel, and independent N(0,1/4) weights at every layer, satisfying the genuine source independent model.')],[SOM,FINITE],[
 st('构造真实独立Gaussian层','Construct actual independent Gaussian layers',r'取有限乘积概率空间，坐标层权重各为$\mathcal N(0,1/4)$；$K=1$的唯一核偏移0，所有频率响应就是该真实实权重。Lean由乘积测度证明坐标律与独立，不假设最终矩值。',r'Use a finite product probability space with coordinate weights N(0,1/4). A K=1 kernel has the sole offset zero, so every frequency response is that real weight. Lean derives coordinate laws and independence from the product measure rather than assuming the final moment.',r'T_l^{(uv)}=W_l',names('quarter_gaussian_coordinate_law','quarter_gaussian_independent')),
 st('比较原指数增加主张','Compare with the source exponential-growth claim',r'真实乘积矩为$(1/4)^L$，两层为$1/16<1/4$一层，且所有频率相同。log恒等式仍正确，增加解释却不成立；多通道C_l=2且μ=0、足够小σ²同样可递减，不能用“approx”自动推出增加。',r'The actual product moment is $(1/4)^L$, so two layers give 1/16<1/4 for one layer, identically at every frequency. The log identity remains valid but the growth interpretation fails. Multichannel C_l=2 with μ=0 and sufficiently small σ² can also decay; the word approximately does not imply growth.',r'(1/4)^2<(1/4)^1',names('actual_unit_kernel_gaussian_depth_moment','actual_gaussian_depth_growth_counterexample'))],
 ('实际Gaussian概率空间、真实K1响应与两层小于一层完整反例；原正确log公式未被否定。','A complete actual-Gaussian-space/K1-response counterexample shows two layers below one. The correct logarithm identity is not refuted.'),original='(2) '+chunks[2],proof='',role='counterexample',assessment='counterexample_recorded',symbols=['kernel-size','som','variance','mean','depth','independence'])
 for i,s,z,e in [(3,'frequency-preference','推论(3)：深度与高频削弱范围','Conclusion (3): depth and high-frequency weakening'),(4,'mean-preference','推论(4)：均值与频率不均衡范围','Conclusion (4): weight means and frequency imbalance')]:
  key='B.'+str(i-2)
  bz=(r'相同层参数且$a_{\rm low}>a_{\rm high}>0$时，SOM比值为$(a_{\rm low}/a_{\rm high})^L$，只证明相对矩不均衡；若μ=0或K=1，各频率矩相同。期望平方模和LLN没有直接给某一次网络“几乎必然”增强低频并削弱高频的结论。' if i==3 else r'若$|R_{\rm low}|>|R_{\rm high}|$且其它参数固定，$|\mu|$增大可增大相对SOM比。但μ=0、K=1或等R频率不产生偏好；表示SOM比不直接证明梯度训练更难学习某频率。')
  be=(r'With equal layer parameters and $a_{\rm low}>a_{\rm high}>0$, the SOM ratio is $(a_{\rm low}/a_{\rm high})^L$, proving relative moment imbalance only. If μ=0 or K=1, frequency moments coincide. A second moment and the law of large numbers do not directly prove that a particular network almost surely strengthens low frequencies and weakens high frequencies.' if i==3 else r'If $|R_{\rm low}|>|R_{\rm high}|$ and other parameters are fixed, larger $|\mu|$ can increase the relative SOM ratio. But μ=0, K=1 or equal-R frequencies have no such preference. A representation-moment ratio does not itself prove greater difficulty in gradient-based learning.')
  add(s,z,e,f'Theorem4.2 interpretation ({i}); Appendix {key}',r'\frac{SOM(\mathbb T_{\rm low})}{SOM(\mathbb T_{\rm high})}=\prod_l\frac{a_{l,\rm low}}{a_{l,\rm high}}',[6,26,27] if i==3 else [6,27],[GAUSS],[SOM,FINITE],[st('区分矩比较与训练推断','Distinguish moment comparison from learning inference',bz,be)],('完整说明条件性矩比较、零偏好边界与未量化训练/概率推断；不伪造一个原文未给的概率定理。','A complete explanation separates conditional moment comparisons, no-preference boundaries and unquantified learning/probability inference, without inventing a probabilistic theorem absent from the source.'),original=f'({i}) '+chunks[i]+'\n\n'+source(key)['original_statement_md'],proof=source(key)['original_proof_md'],proofpages=source(key)['source_pages'],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',symbols=['phase-sum','mean','variance','som','depth'])
 add('kernel-preference','推论(5)：大核缓解不均衡的反例','Conclusion (5): a counterexample to large-kernel alleviation','Theorem4.2 interpretation (5); B.3',r'\frac{SOM(T_{00})}{SOM(T_{40})}=K^2+1',[6,27],[GAUSS,('真实模型M=N=8、L=1、μ=1、σ²=1，比较K=2与K=4。','The actual model has M=N=8, L=1, μ=1 and σ²=1; compare K=2 with K=4.')],[SOM,FINITE],[st('计算实际两个频率的R','Compute actual R at two frequencies',r'DC每个相位1，R00=K²；频率(4,0)的t相位是(−1)^t，偶K=2/4相消，R40=0。因此SOM00=K⁴+K²，SOM40=K²，真实独立Gaussian矩比为K²+1。',r'At DC every phase is one, so R00=K². At (4,0), the t phase is (−1)^t, which cancels for even K=2 or 4, giving R40=0. Thus SOM00=K⁴+K² and SOM40=K², with actual independent-Gaussian moment ratio K²+1.',r'K=2:\ 5,\qquad K=4:\ 17'),st('保留原子句并限定影响','Retain the clause and limit the impact',r'大核使该比从5增到17，原B.3普遍缓解不均衡的解释缺条件。这里K与R按真实偏移一起改变，不能把R固定后以K²σ²项增长替原网络解释作证。单核矩公式本身仍成立。',r'The ratio rises from five to seventeen with the larger kernel, so the universal alleviation explanation in B.3 lacks conditions. K and R change together through actual offsets; holding R fixed and increasing K²σ² does not prove the source network interpretation. The kernel-moment formula remains valid.')],('完整真实核人读反例；具体K2/K4实例未独立机器编码，不影响已验证的通用Gaussian核矩。','A complete actual-kernel human counterexample; the concrete K2/K4 instance has not yet been separately encoded and does not affect the verified generic Gaussian kernel moments.'),original='(5) '+chunks[5]+'\n\n'+source('B.3')['original_statement_md'],proof=source('B.3')['original_proof_md'],proofpages=[27],role='counterexample',assessment='counterexample_recorded',leanrole='none',symbols=['phase-sum','kernel-size','mean','variance','som'])

def build_defects(p,add):
 add('zero-padding','Theorem 4.3：真实相关Gaussian padding反例','Theorem 4.3: actual correlated-Gaussian padding counterexample','Theorem4.3 Eqs8–9; A.5 Eqs33–39',r'SOM(H_{uv})-SOM(G_{uv})=a^2\tau_{uv}^2',[6,22,23],[('原陈述仅各像素边缘N(a,σ²)，没有像素独立假设；u+v≠0，DC另有相等句。原文字指定edge zero-padding。','The statement specifies only pixel marginals N(a,σ²), without independence, and u+v≠0, with a separate DC equality. The prose specifies edge zero padding.')],[GRID,DFT,SOM,('按原edge-padding文字，旧矩形原值保留，其余位置0。打印Eq8只给右下角零域，漏两条边带，原错分段保留，规范算子用otherwise=0。','Under the stated edge-padding prose, retain the old rectangle and put zero elsewhere. Printed Equation (8) covers only the bottom-right zero region, omitting two strips. Preserve that printing error; the canonical operator uses otherwise=0.')],[
 st('区分原边缘条件与证明iid条件','Separate source marginal conditions from proof iid conditions',r'A.5以$i.i.d.$像素计算方差，把不同像素交叉协方差置0；这不是仅同Gaussian边缘的结论。若确实独立，则负相位有限矩形和给均值$aP_M(z)P_N(w)$、方差$MN\sigma^2$，旧非DC均值0，得到原非DC差值。',r'A.5 computes variance using iid pixels and zero cross covariances. This does not follow from equal Gaussian marginals alone. Under actual independence, the finite rectangle gives mean $aP_M(z)P_N(w)$ and variance $MN\sigma^2$, while the old non-DC mean is zero, yielding the stated difference.'),
 st('计算同一Gaussian填满真实输入','Compute an actual input filled by the same Gaussian',r'取$M=N=2,M^{\prime}=N^{\prime}=3$，每个旧像素都等于同一$U\sim\mathcal N(0,q)$，q>0。各边缘满足原a=0条件。旧2×2在(1,1)的DFT为0；真实padding后的DFT为$U(1+z)^2$，$z=e^{-2\pi i/3}$，$|1+z|^2=1$，所以SOM差q>0而原a²τ²=0。此频率两分母均非零，u+v≠0。',r'Take M=N=2 and M′=N′=3, with every original pixel equal to the same U~N(0,q), q>0. Each marginal satisfies a=0. The old 2×2 DFT at (1,1) is zero. After actual padding it is $U(1+z)^2$, where $z=e^{-2\pi i/3}$ and $|1+z|^2=1$. The SOM difference is q>0, while a²τ²=0. Both quotient denominators are nonzero and u+v≠0.',r'SOM(H_{11})-SOM(G_{11})=q>0=a^2\tau_{11}^2',names('edge_pad_original','edge_pad_zero','edge_pad_constant_dft','padded_phase_normSq_one','actual_correlated_padding_counterexample')),
 st('限定反例及正确DC句','Limit the counterexample and retain the correct DC clause',r'DC是所有像素总和，边缘补0不改变总和，故原DC相等仍成立，不用它作为非DC反例。原式τ在单坐标0也有商域问题，用有限和可解释合法值；这和相关像素反例分开。',r'DC is the sum of all pixels, which zero padding does not change, so the original DC equality remains valid and is not used as a non-DC counterexample. The printed τ also has domain problems on coordinate axes; finite sums supply its legitimate values, separately from the correlated-pixel counterexample.')],
 ('原边缘Gaussian前提下，真实空间padding/DFT/概率矩反例完整机器验证；独立像素的条件性等式有完整人读推导，未偷偷加iid修原命题。','The actual spatial-padding/DFT/probability-moment counterexample is fully formalized under the source marginal-Gaussian premise. The conditional iid equality has a complete human derivation and is not presented as the original theorem with an added premise.'),keys=['main-theorem-4.3','A.5'],role='counterexample',assessment='partially_refuted',symbols=['grid','input-feature','input-spectrum','padding','som','mean','variance','padding-factor'])
 add('upsampling','Theorem 4.4：真实零插值的重复频谱','Theorem 4.4: repeated spectra under actual zero insertion','Theorem4.4 Eqs10–11; A.6 Eqs40–42',r'H_{u+jM_0,v+kN_0}^{(c)}=G_{uv}^{(c)},\quad0\le j,k<r',[6,23,24],[('M0,N0>0，正整数ratio=r，M=rM0、N=rN0；只在r倍坐标插入原值，其余0，各通道独立应用。','M0,N0>0, integer ratio r>0, M=rM0 and N=rN0. Insert original values at coordinates divisible by r, zero elsewhere, applying the operation to every channel.')],[GRID,DFT],[
 st('定义真实插值位置','Define actual insertion positions',r'位置映射$(m,n)\mapsto(rm,rn)$进入更大循环网格。因旧代表元范围m<M0,n<N0且r>0，它injective；散射求和在插入点回收原值，其余点为0，没有预先假设变换等式。',r'The position map $(m,n)\mapsto(rm,rn)$ enters the larger cyclic grid. Bounds m<M0 and n<N0 with r>0 prove injectivity. A scatter sum recovers the original value at inserted points and gives zero elsewhere; the transform identity is not assumed.',r'\widetilde F(rm,rn)=F(m,n)',names('insert_grid_injective','zero_insert_original','zero_insert_elsewhere')),
 st('计算字符在插入位置的值','Compute characters at inserted positions',r'$e^{-2\pi i[u(rm)/(rM0)+v(rn)/(rN0)]}=e^{-2\pi i[um/M0+vn/N0]}$，故大网格频率仅经模M0,N0余数作用于旧数据。代入真实插值DFT，所有非插入位置0，得到全频重复。',r'At inserted positions, $e^{-2\pi i[u(rm)/(rM0)+v(rn)/(rN0)]}=e^{-2\pi i[um/M0+vn/N0]}$. A large-grid frequency therefore acts on old data through its remainders modulo M0 and N0. Substitution into the actual inserted DFT removes all zero positions and proves repetition at every frequency.',r'H_{u,v}=G_{u\bmod M_0,v\bmod N_0}',names('inserted_character','zero_insert_dft_repeats')),
 st('适配原s/t频率分块','Adapt the original s/t frequency blocks',r'原1≤s,t≤r改记j=s−1,k=t−1，u+jM0<M、v+kN0<N。真实frequencyBlock的模余数就是u,v，直接应用全频式得到原Eq11全部块，所有通道相同。',r'Write j=s−1 and k=t−1 for the source 1≤s,t≤r, giving u+jM0<M and v+kN0<N. The actual frequencyBlock remainders are u and v, so the all-frequency identity gives every block of Equation (11), identically for each channel.',r'H_{u+jM_0,v+kN_0}=G_{u,v}',names('frequency_block_remainder','actual_zero_insert_frequency_blocks'))],
 ('真实位置算子、字符约分、全频重复与原频率块上下界完整验证。','The actual spatial operator, character identity, all-frequency repetition and source block bounds are fully verified.'),keys=['main-theorem-4.4','A.6'],symbols=['grid','input-feature','input-spectrum','upsampling-ratio','upsampling'])
 a7=source('A.7')['original_proof_md']
 first,rest=a7.split('For any other frequency component',1)
 other='For any other frequency component'+rest
 other,norm=other.split('And $',1);norm='And $'+norm
 add('shift-setup','频率移位设置的幅值范围','Magnitude scope of the frequency-shift setting','Theorem4.5 preceding setup',r'H_1^*=(1-A)G_1,\quad H_2^*=(1+\overline A)G_2',[6,7],[('原A=αexp(iφ)、α>0、φ<π/2；不擅加φ下界或α上界。','The source uses A=αexp(iφ), α>0 and φ<π/2; no lower bound on φ or upper bound on α is added.')],[(r'设G1,G2非0，幅值改变由$|1-A|^2=1-2\alpha\cos\varphi+\alpha^2$与$|1+\overline A|^2=1+2\alpha\cos\varphi+\alpha^2$判断。',r'For nonzero G1,G2, changes follow from $|1-A|^2=1-2\alpha\cos\varphi+\alpha^2$ and $|1+\overline A|^2=1+2\alpha\cos\varphi+\alpha^2$.')],[st('保留原范围并核对减幅','Retain the scope and check the claimed decrease',r'原正α与单边φ<π/2不足保证第一个幅值下降。取φ=0、α=3，满足原条件但$|1-A|=2>1$。真正减幅需要$\alpha<2\cos\varphi$且cosφ>0，这只用于解释缺口，不加入原命题冒充已证。',r'Positive α and the one-sided φ<π/2 do not ensure the first magnitude decreases. At φ=0 and α=3, source conditions hold but $|1-A|=2>1$. A true decrease needs $\alpha<2\cos\varphi$ with cosφ>0; these conditions explain the gap rather than being inserted into the original claim.',r'\alpha=3,\ \varphi=0:\quad|1-A|=2>1')],('原设置的减幅解释有明确人读反例；下条一步GD反例独立选α=1/4、φ=0，确实满足期望减/增幅。','The source decrease interpretation has an explicit human counterexample. The separate one-step GD counterexample uses α=1/4 and φ=0, satisfying the intended decrease/increase.'),original=source('main-theorem-4.5')['original_statement_md'].split('According to Corollary 3.3')[0],proof='',role='counterexample',assessment='counterexample_recorded',leanrole='none',symbols=['shift-amplitude','shift-phase','input-spectrum','target-spectrum'])
 add('one-step-fitting','Theorem 4.5：真实两层一步GD反例','Theorem 4.5: an actual two-layer one-step GD counterexample','Theorem4.5; A.7 Eqs43–50',r'\operatorname{Im}H_{10}^{\mathrm{updated}}=-2c(1+c)\ne0,\quad c=2\eta\alpha>0',[7,24,25],[LINEAR,('M=N=4,K=2,L=2，单通道，两层identity δ核，bias0、输入δ。取f1=(0,1)、f2=(1,0)、α=1/4、φ=0，原loss仅两个选定频率。','M=N=4,K=2,L=2, one channel, identity delta kernels, zero biases and delta input. Let f1=(0,1), f2=(1,0), α=1/4 and φ=0, with the original loss using only the two selected frequencies.')],[DFT,CAS,FINITE,('目标谱在两个所选频率为1−α、1+α，在负频率取对应共轭，其余1；Hermitian逆DFT给真实实目标图像，但loss不额外加入共轭项。','The target has values 1−α and 1+α at the selected frequencies, their conjugates at negative frequencies, and one elsewhere. Hermitian inverse DFT yields a real target image without adding conjugate terms to the loss.')],[
 st('逐项满足原约束43–46','Satisfy source constraints (43)–(46)',r'输入δ的所有DFT为1，故Eq43两λ均1；Eq44相位$[(1)(1)/4+(1)(-1)/4]\pi/2=0$；identity核每频响应1，Eq45层积1；两层bypass范数和各2，Eq46成立。α=1/4也给真实下降/上升。',r'Every DFT of the delta input is one, so both λ values in (43) are one. Equation (44) gives phase $[(1)(1)/4+(1)(-1)/4]\pi/2=0$. Identity kernels have unit response, so (45) has product one and both bypass-norm sums in (46) are two. α=1/4 also gives the intended decrease/increase.',r'\lambda_1=\lambda_2=1,\quad\phi=0,\quad\mathbb T_1=\mathbb T_2=1',names('source_constraint43','source_constraint44','source_constraint45','source_constraint46','completed_target_image_real','completed_target_selected_frequencies')),
 st('求实际四坐标实梯度','Compute the actual four-coordinate real gradient',r'核$(a,b,c,d)$真实响应为$T_{01}=a+c+i(b+d)$、$T_{10}=a+b+i(c+d)$，由实际二维偏移核DFT推出。原两频loss在另一层identity处等于显式实平方和，对四个实坐标的HasDerivAt给$(0,-2\alpha,2\alpha,0)$。换层对称保证两层梯度相同；非DC loss对bias无贡献。',r'The actual kernel $(a,b,c,d)$ has $T_{01}=a+c+i(b+d)$ and $T_{10}=a+b+i(c+d)$, derived from the two-dimensional offset response. With the other layer fixed at identity, the original two-frequency loss is an explicit real sum of squares. HasDerivAt in the four real coordinates gives $(0,-2\alpha,2\alpha,0)$. Layer exchange gives the same gradient in both layers; non-DC loss has no bias contribution.',r'\nabla W_1=\nabla W_2=(0,-2\alpha,2\alpha,0)',names('actual_response01','actual_response10','actual_real_loss_identity_layer','actual_gradient00','actual_gradient01','actual_gradient10','actual_gradient11','actual_real_loss_layer_exchange')),
 st('计算实际两层更新后输出','Compute the actual output after updating both layers',r'任意η>0后每层核为$(1,c,-c,0)$，c=2ηα>0。频率(1,0)响应为$1+c-ic$，实际空间两层DFT为$(1+c-ic)^2$，虚部$-2c(1+c)\ne0$，而目标1+α为实数。因此没有任意正步长能让原两频loss一步到0。',r'After any η>0, each kernel is $(1,c,-c,0)$ with c=2ηα>0. The (1,0) response is $1+c-ic$; the actual spatial two-layer DFT is $(1+c-ic)^2$, with imaginary part $-2c(1+c)\ne0$. The target 1+α is real. Thus no positive learning rate reaches zero original two-frequency loss in one step.',r'H_{10}^{\rm updated}=(1+c-ic)^2\ne1+\alpha',names('actual_two_layer_spectrum','actual_spatial_one_step_not_target'))],
 ('实际实核→二维DFT→空间两层网络→原两频loss→坐标梯度→两层更新→非零残差完整反例；原source约束逐项验证。没有仅用末端标量替代实际网络。','The complete counterexample connects real kernels, actual 2D DFT, the spatial two-layer network, the original two-frequency loss, coordinate gradients, both layer updates and a nonzero residual, with each source constraint verified.'),original=source('main-theorem-4.5')['original_statement_md'],proof=first,proofpages=[24,25],role='counterexample',assessment='partially_refuted',symbols=['grid','kernel','kernel-response','cascade-response','loss','gradient','learning-rate','shift-amplitude','shift-phase','target-spectrum','depth'])
 add('first-order-product','A.7：有限更新不可等同一阶层积','A.7: a finite product update is not its first-order change','A.7 Eq48',r'(T_2+\Delta T_2)(T_1+\Delta T_1)-T_2T_1=T_2\Delta T_1+\Delta T_2T_1+\Delta T_2\Delta T_1',[24,25],[('层响应可为复数；原Eq48首先明确≈并标First order approximation，后文却据此求精确零loss一步。','Responses may be complex. Equation (48) first explicitly uses ≈ and labels a first-order approximation, then uses it to claim exact one-step zero loss.')],[CAS],[st('保留所有有限乘积项','Retain every finite product term',r'两层直接展开有交叉项$\Delta T_2\Delta T_1$。一般L层对所有非空更新层子集求和，一阶式只保留单元素子集。这个差可随η小但不等于0，除非另有能推出交叉项为0的原条件。',r'Two-layer expansion includes $\Delta T_2\Delta T_1$. At general finite depth, the exact expansion sums over all nonempty subsets of updated layers, while the first-order expression keeps only singleton subsets. The error may be small with η but need not be zero.',r'\Delta(T_2T_1)=T_2\Delta T_1+\Delta T_2T_1+\Delta T_2\Delta T_1',names('product_update_exact','dropped_product_counterexample')),st('连接原一步目标','Connect this with the one-step claim',r'上一条实际两层反例说明原43–46没有消去这些交叉效应；修复证明时应保留≈，不能把近似等号变精确来完成错误原一步命题。',r'The actual two-layer counterexample shows that (43)–(46) do not eliminate these effects. A repaired proof must retain the approximation symbol and cannot turn it into an exact equality to prove the false one-step claim.')],('精确两因子代数与非零交叉项反例形式化；真实原网络一步反例在独立目标链接。','Exact two-factor algebra and a nonzero cross-term witness are formalized; the actual source-network counterexample is linked separately.'),original=r'According to Corollary 3.4, after a single step of gradient descent, the change of $\mathbb T^{(uv)(L:1)}$ can be computed as follows. $$\Delta\mathbb T^{(uv)(L:1)}\approx\sum_{l=1}^L\mathbb T^{(L:l+1)(uv)}\Delta T^{(l,uv)}\mathbb T^{(l-1:1)(uv)}\quad\text{//First order approximation}.\tag{48}$$',proof='',role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['cascade-response','gradient','learning-rate','depth'])
 add('shift-other-frequencies','A.7：其他频率线性系数及步长消约范围','A.7: other-frequency coefficients and learning-rate cancellation','A.7 Eqs51–55',r'\Delta\mathbb T_{uv}=a_1\Delta\mathbb T_{f_1}+a_2\Delta\mathbb T_{f_2}',[25],[('原文称a1,a2在learning中不变，且用−a1A+a2Ā除以自身；保留原无非零前提的论证范围。','The source says a1,a2 stay unchanged during learning, and cancels −a1A+a2Ā against itself; retain the argument without inserting a missing nonzero premise.')],[CAS,FINITE],[st('辨析冻结状态与整个训练过程','Distinguish a frozen state from an entire training process',r'冻结某一状态的一阶Jacobian可给线性响应关系，但层积导数系数依赖当前其它层权重。原文字未给足以使a1,a2整个训练保持恒定的条件，Eq48近似也不能转成Eq51的全程精确式。',r'A frozen-state first-order Jacobian can give linear response relations, but product derivatives depend on other layers’ current weights. The source does not provide conditions making a1,a2 constant throughout training, and the approximation in (48) cannot become an exact all-training identity in (51).'),st('保留消约的零域','Retain the zero-cancellation boundary',r'若$-a_1A+a_2\overline A=0$，Eq55中相同比值为0/0，不能取消。正弦商也须用有限χ处理；即便在非零消约域，得到的步长来自一阶目标，不保证原多层精确一步loss0。',r'If $-a_1A+a_2\overline A=0$, Equation (55) contains 0/0 and cannot cancel it. Sine quotients likewise need the finite χ interpretation. Even away from these boundaries, the derived step comes from a first-order target and does not guarantee exact one-step zero loss in a multilayer network.')],('完整解释原固定系数/消约/近似域缺口；没有原明确可证全称目标的完整Lean证据，不造额外前提后称原式已证明。','A complete account of the fixed-coefficient, cancellation and approximation gaps; there is no complete Lean evidence for a well-defined universal source target, and no added premises are presented as proving the original.'),original=other,proof=other,proofpages=[25],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='none',symbols=['cascade-response','cross-frequency','learning-rate','shift-amplitude','shift-phase'])
 add('gradient-norm','A.7：Parseval归一化与Eq56–57','A.7: Parseval normalization and Equations (56)–(57)','A.7 Eqs56–57; mainEq12',r'\sum_{t,s}|r_{ts}|^2=MN\sum_{u,v}|q_{uv}|^2,\quad q=\frac1{MN}\widehat r_{\rm positive}',[7,25,26],[('r是实空间核梯度补0到完整M×N网格，q=(MN)−1乘正相位DFT；原MN规范不变。','r is the real kernel gradient extended by zero to the M×N grid, and q is the positive-phase DFT divided by MN; retain the source normalization.')],[DFT,SOM],[st('按实际DFT计算范数','Compute the norm using the actual DFT',r'二维Parseval为$\sum|\widehat r|^2=MN\sum|r|^2$。q=(MN)−1$\widehat r$故$\sum|r|^2=MN\sum|q|^2$；原Eq56漏这个MN（若另采用Wirtinger需再说明因子2），不能由原梯度名取消尺度。',r'Two-dimensional Parseval is $\sum|\widehat r|^2=MN\sum|r|^2$. Since q=(MN)−1$\widehat r$, $\sum|r|^2=MN\sum|q|^2$. Equation (56) omits MN; a Wirtinger convention may additionally change a factor of two and must be stated explicitly.',r'\sum|r|^2=MN\sum|q|^2',names('dft2_parseval_normSq','dft2_parseval_pair')),st('区分尺度修复与错误一步结论','Separate normalization repair from the false one-step claim',r'固定其余条件时梯度随α线性、范数随|α|可成立，但原Eq57中间印$\eta\sqrt{\|\Delta W\|^2}$自指，应由梯度范数推理。修复归一化与笔误不能挽救已被真实网络反驳的一步目标，Eq12成本依其一步η推导须单列适用范围。',r'With other conditions fixed, the gradient may scale linearly in α and its norm in |α|. The middle line of (57) instead prints the self-reference $\eta\sqrt{\|\Delta W\|^2}$ where a gradient norm is needed. Fixing normalization and that typo cannot rescue the refuted one-step claim; the cost in (12), derived through its one-step η, needs a separate scope assessment.')],('实际二维Parseval完整验证；原Eq56尺度错误和Eq57自指已解释，原Eq12作为精确一步成本不能由这些局部修复认作原全命题通过。','Actual two-dimensional Parseval is fully verified. The scale error in (56) and self-reference in (57) are explained; these local repairs do not prove (12) as an exact one-step cost theorem.'),original=norm,proof=norm,proofpages=[25,26],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['grid','gradient','loss','learning-rate','shift-amplitude','kernel-size'])

def build_analysis(p,add):
 for s,z,e,key,bz,be in [
 ('padding-interpretation','padding后低频趋势的范围','Scope of the low-frequency trend after padding','main-theorem-4.3',r'真正独立像素、受控相同均值模型中，原SOM差由$a^2|P_M(z)P_N(w)|^2$决定；a=0时所有这些差为0，原边缘条件下又有相关反例。仅τ大不自动推出含其它层矩阵、非线性和bias的训练网络必然编码低频。',r'For genuinely independent pixels with controlled common mean, the SOM difference is $a^2|P_M(z)P_N(w)|^2$. At a=0 these differences vanish, and the original marginal-only premise also admits the correlated counterexample. Large τ alone does not prove inevitable low-frequency encoding in a trained network with other matrices, nonlinearities and biases.'),
 ('upsampling-interpretation','重复DC信号与表示/辨别推理','Repeated DC signals and representation/discrimination inference','main-theorem-4.4',r'真实零插值把输入DC精确复制到所有(r块)对应频率，这是已证等式。后继线性层输出还乘各频率响应，零响应可抑制复制信号。因此“hurt representation”及“may provide clues”是作者解释/可能用途，不是由重复谱推出的普遍容量或分类定理。',r'Actual zero insertion exactly copies input DC into the corresponding frequencies of every block, an established identity. Subsequent layers multiply by their frequency responses and zero responses may suppress those copies. “Hurt representation” and “may provide clues” are interpretations and potential uses, rather than universal capacity or discrimination theorems.'),
 ('shift-difficulty-interpretation','小频差与优化难度解释','Small frequency shifts and optimization-difficulty inference','main-theorem-4.5',r'原成本指标是一次权重改变范数，依赖所选步长、梯度、输入频率、层积和原近似推导。因为原一步零loss子句被实际反例否定，不能仅由Eq12商推出任何真实优化过程对小位移必然更难；正文/附录移频实验另保留为观察。',r'The source cost metric is a one-step weight-change norm, depending on the step size, gradient, input spectrum, layer products and approximation. Since the exact one-step-zero-loss clause is refuted, the quotient in (12) alone does not establish universally harder actual optimization at smaller shifts. The frequency-shift experiments remain observations.')]:
  text=source(key)['original_proof_md']
  add(s,z,e,'Unnumbered main interpretation following '+key,r'\mathrm{frequency\ identity}\Rightarrow\mathrm{interpretation}',[6] if key!='main-theorem-4.5' else [7],[LINEAR],[DFT,CAS,SOM],[st('保留数学式与解释的距离','Separate identities from interpretations',bz,be)],('完整原未编号论证与适用范围；未定义的容量/难度全称主张不伪造成机器定理。','The complete unnumbered argument and its scope are retained; undefined universal capacity/difficulty claims are not invented as machine theorems.'),original=text,proof=text,proofpages=[6] if key!='main-theorem-4.5' else [7],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='none',symbols=['input-spectrum','kernel-response','cascade-response','som'])
 add('natural-input','B.4：输入谱幅值与输出推理范围','B.4: input-spectrum magnitude and the output inference','B.4; Section5.1 unnumbered argument',r'h^{(uv)}=\mathbb T^{(uv)(L:1)}g^{(uv)}+\delta_{uv}\beta',[8,27],[LINEAR],[DFT,CAS],[st('保留输入与响应两个因素','Retain both the input and the response',r'非DC有$h=\mathbb Tg$。单通道$|h|=|\mathbb T||g|$，多通道只自动有上界$\|h\|\le\|\mathbb T\|_{\rm op}\|g\|$，没有响应下界不能推出大输入给大输出。真实零核令$\mathbb T=0$，任意非DC大g仍h=0；DC还需保留bias。',r'At non-DC, h=𝕋g. A single channel gives $|h|=|\mathbb T||g|$; multiple channels only automatically give $\|h\|\le\|\mathbb T\|_{\rm op}\|g\|$. Without a response lower bound, a large input does not imply a large output. Actual zero kernels make 𝕋=0, so arbitrarily large non-DC g still gives h=0. DC additionally retains bias.'),st('区分外引自然图像统计与推断','Separate cited image statistics from inference',r'Ruderman关于自然图像低频占优/Power-law是外引经验背景，本源未给它的证明。它可解释实测输入谱，不能独自补足T方向、非零响应或训练收敛条件；本文实验趋势范围单列。',r'The Ruderman citation on low-frequency dominance and power laws is external empirical background without a proof here. It may describe observed input spectra, but does not supply nonzero responses, favorable directions or convergence conditions. Experimental trends are recorded separately.')],('完整人读范围与真实零核反例；没有把经验Power-law或训练趋势伪造成全称机器定理。','A complete human scope analysis and actual-zero-kernel counterexample, without presenting empirical power laws or learning trends as universal machine theorems.'),keys=['B.4'],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',symbols=['input-spectrum','cascade-response','bias','depth'])
 mainlayer=r'We also conducted experiments to measure the effects of large absolute mean values on layers with different depth. Results in Appendix C.8 show that no matter which layer had parameters of a large absolute mean value, there was no significant difference in weakening the encoding of high-frequency components. It was because different convolutional layers, including both shallow and deep layers, theoretically had similar roles in affecting the frequency representation of the entire network, according to Corollary 3.3.'
 add('layer-placement','均值所在层与层作用相同的范围','Scope of mean placement and equal layer roles','Section5.1 PDF8; C.8 PDF33',r'\mathbb T=T_L\cdots T_1',[8,33],[LINEAR],[CAS],[st('辨析单通道乘积与多通道顺序','Distinguish scalar products from matrix order',r'单通道独立SOM的$\prod_la_l$对因子排列对称，所以仅在同其它层参数、同尺寸等受控条件下，改变相同μ因子所在层可不变。原Cor3.3是矩阵有序积，矩阵不可交换，bias通过不同后缀传播，因此不推出所有层的作用总相同。',r'The independent single-channel SOM product $\prod_la_l$ is symmetric in its factors, so moving the same mean factor can be invariant under controlled equal-other-parameter and equal-size conditions. Corollary 3.3 itself is an ordered matrix product; matrices need not commute and biases propagate through different suffixes. It therefore does not imply universally equal roles for all layers.'),st('保留实验结论的对象','Retain the object of the experimental conclusion',r'C.8比较五个同架构随机网络及全零均值基线，原“no significant difference”是这组实验的观察。不能把该观察外推成任意通道、非线性、bias网络的参数位置定理。',r'C.8 compares five random networks of the same architecture with an all-zero-mean baseline. Its “no significant difference” is an observation in those experiments, not a theorem for arbitrary channel widths, nonlinearities or biases.')],('完整原未编号推断及其单通道条件解释；原多通道全称层作用相同不由Cor3.3自动推出。','The original unnumbered inference is retained with its scalar conditional explanation; universally equal multichannel layer roles do not automatically follow from Corollary 3.3.'),original=mainlayer,proof=mainlayer,proofpages=[8],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',symbols=['cascade-response','depth','channels','mean','bias'])
 c6=r'In this section, we discuss the problem of the curse of dimension, when we compute the cosine similarity of two high-dimensional vectors with as many as $32^2$, $64^2$ or $224^2$ dimensions. In general, for each pair of extremely high-dimensional vectors, it’s hard for these vectors to have very high cosine similarity. It is because even if the noisy differences between many pairs of dimensions can be ignored, in the process of calculating the sum of squares, these noisy differences will accumulate. Therefore, the cosine similarity of two extremely high-dimensional vectors will not be particularly large.'
 add('cosine-dimension','C.6：高维余弦解释的条件范围','C.6: conditional scope of the high-dimensional cosine explanation','C.6 PDF32',r'\cos(x,y)=\frac{\langle x,y\rangle}{\|x\|\|y\|}',[32],[('原段没有给噪声分布、独立性、信号尺度或概率界；余弦只在两向量非零时定义。','The paragraph specifies no noise distribution, independence, signal scale or probability bound. Cosine is defined only for nonzero vectors.')],[('余弦是正规化内积，受角度而非维数单独决定。','Cosine is the normalized inner product; angles, rather than dimension alone, determine it.')],[st('核对维数本身能否限制余弦','Check whether dimension alone bounds cosine',r'任意正维数取$x=y=(1,\ldots,1)$，余弦恰为1。即使每坐标差为ε，取$y=(1+\epsilon)x$、1+ε>0，余弦仍1；平方差随维数积累而不迫使余弦下降。',r'At any positive dimension, x=y=(1,…,1) has cosine exactly one. Even with coordinatewise difference ε, y=(1+ε)x and 1+ε>0 still have cosine one. Squared differences can accumulate with dimension without lowering cosine.',r'\cos(x,(1+\epsilon)x)=1'),st('保持原经验解释的范围','Retain the scope of the empirical explanation',r'若要概率化“hard”，须给信号/噪声模型及定量事件；原段没有给这些，本文保留为未量化解释，反例只否定其按维数全称读取，不替原文添加新的噪声定理。',r'A probabilistic meaning of “hard” needs a signal/noise model and a quantitative event. These are absent here, so retain the paragraph as an unquantified explanation. The example only rejects a universal dimension-only reading and does not insert a new noise theorem.')],('完整未编号解释与明确维数全称读取反例；无原定义的概率目标可认作已机器证明。','The complete unnumbered explanation and an explicit counterexample to a universal dimension-only reading are retained; there is no source-defined probabilistic target to report as machine-proved.'),original=c6,proof=c6,proofpages=[32],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='none',symbols=['cosine','grid'])
 c7=r'''Assumption 4.1 shows that in early training of a DNN, all elements in $T^{(l,uv)}$ are irrelevant to each other, and $\forall l\ne l'$, elements in $T^{(l,uv)}$ and $T^{(l',uv)}$ are irrelevant to each other. In this section, we further conducted experiments to verify that such irrelevant relationships also existed in a fully trained DNN. To this end, we constructed a cascaded convolutional auto-encoder by using the VGG-16 as the encoder network. The decoder network contained ten convolutional layers, where the 1st, 3rd, 5th, 7th, and 9th layers were traditional convolutional layers, and the 2nd, 4th, 6th, 8th, and 10th layers were upconvolutional layers. Each convolutional/upconvolutional layer applied zero-paddings and was followed by a batch normalization layer and an ReLU layer. The network was trained on the Tiny-ImageNet dataset using the mean squared error (MSE) loss for image reconstruction.

Let the above auto-encoder be trained to convergence. Then, we computed the Pearson’s correlation coefficient between each random pair of variables $|\Delta T^{(l,uv)}_{d_1c_1}|$ and $|\Delta T^{(l,uv)}_{d_2c_2}|$ through different images, denoted by $r(|\Delta T^{(l,uv)}_{d_1c_1}|,|\Delta T^{(l,uv)}_{d_2c_2}|)$, to measure the relevance between two elements $T^{(l,uv)}_{d_1c_1}$ and $T^{(l,uv)}_{d_2c_2}$ in $T^{(l,uv)}$. Here, $\Delta T^{(l,uv)}$ denoted the change of $T^{(l,uv)}$ when we updated parameters $\mathbf W$ for a single gradient-descent step on a single input sample. Results in Table 1 show that even when the network was fully trained, different elements in $T^{(l,uv)}$ had low Pearson’s correlation coefficient $r$. This proved that our assumption that all elements in $T^{(l,uv)}$ were irrelevant to each other was reasonable. The last three convolutional layers in the decoder showed a larger Pearson’s correlation coefficient, because network parameters close to the output layer had been converged to the principle feature direction of each category. Nevertheless, our experiments showed that for most layers, we could keep Assumption 4.1, which enabled to us to prove that convolution operations in these layers weakened high-frequency components.'''
 add('trained-independence','C.7：低Pearson相关与独立假设的对象差异','C.7: object mismatch between low Pearson correlation and independence','C.7 title Assumption3.1; body Assumption4.1; Table1',r'r(|\Delta T_1|,|\Delta T_2|)\approx0',[32,33],[('原实测对象是不同样本诱发的|ΔT|，不是随机初始化T；Pearson系数低不是独立定义。','The measured objects are magnitudes |ΔT| induced by different inputs, rather than randomly initialized T. A low Pearson coefficient is not the definition of independence.')],[SOM,GAUSS],[st('保留测量对象与概率对象','Retain the measured and probabilistic objects',r'对一个训练好网络，原权重T固定，而每图像一次更新ΔT随图像随机。|ΔT|的近零线性相关不能直接推出T的层间独立或所需共轭二阶乘积分解；零相关也不足一般独立（例如U与U²−EU²）。',r'In a trained fixed network, T is fixed, while a one-image update ΔT varies with the input image. Near-zero linear correlation of |ΔT| does not directly establish layerwise independence of T or the required conjugated second-product factorization. Zero correlation also need not imply independence, as with U and U²−EU².'),st('对齐原标题、正文与模型范围','Align the source heading, text and model scope',r'C.7标题原写Assumption3.1而正文谈4.1，保留两个标签供检索。实测网络含zero-padding、upsampling、BN、ReLU，不满足精确无activation circular cascade；实测相关可作为经验支持，但不能把原独立证明的所有前提自动恢复。',r'The C.7 heading says Assumption 3.1 while the text discusses 4.1; retain both labels for search. The measured network includes zero padding, upsampling, batch normalization and ReLU, outside the exact activation-free circular cascade. Measured correlations may support an empirical interpretation, but do not automatically restore every premise of the independent-model proof.')],('完整原未编号适配推理与对象/条件范围；原Table1统计值不被当作独立性机器证明。','The complete unnumbered adaptation inference is retained with its object and condition scopes; Table 1 statistics are not treated as machine evidence of independence.'),original=c7,proof=c7,proofpages=[32,33],role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='none',symbols=['kernel-response','gradient','pearson','independence','depth'])
 add('external-gaussian-closure','外引：Gaussian线性组合与LLN作用域','External claims: Gaussian linear combinations and LLN scope','A.4 Tse–Viswanath; main5 and B.1 LLN',r'\sum_j a_jX_j\ \text{is Gaussian under joint Gaussianity}',[5,19,26,27],[('边缘各为Gaussian不足推出任意线性和Gaussian；原source的真正独立初始化读取可提供联合Gaussian。','Gaussian marginals alone do not guarantee a Gaussian linear sum; the source genuine independent-initialization reading supplies joint Gaussianity.')],[SOM,GAUSS],[st('连接外引所需联合条件','Connect the joint conditions of the cited claim',r'独立Gaussian的乘积律是联合Gaussian，连续实线性组合在$\mathbb C\simeq\mathbb R^2$仍Gaussian；已从实际独立实权重证明。原Tse–Viswanath陈述按边缘读取时缺联合条件，不能只用Gaussian一词替代它。',r'The product of independent Gaussian laws is jointly Gaussian, and continuous real linear combinations remain Gaussian in $\mathbb C\simeq\mathbb R^2$. This is proved for actual independent real weights. A marginal-only reading of the cited Tse–Viswanath statement lacks the required joint condition.',r'T=\sum_j a_jW_j',names('gaussian_weighted_isGaussian')),st('区分LLN与单个网络概率','Distinguish LLN from a single-network probability claim',r'LLN可支持重复独立网络样本的经验平均估计SOM；有限深度SOM乘积公式本身不需要LLN。原没有给随机层log可积、同分布或几乎必然增长率条件，不能由引名推单个网络必然频率削弱。',r'The law of large numbers may support estimating SOM by averaging independent sampled networks. The finite-depth SOM product itself does not need LLN. The source does not state integrability, identical-law or almost-sure growth-rate conditions for random layer logs; naming LLN does not establish deterministic weakening in a particular network.')],('实际Gaussian闭包有机器证明；LLN外引仅登记其原使用与必要scope，未声称本文或本库完整形式化原未量化LLN应用。','Actual Gaussian closure has machine evidence. LLN is recorded as an external use with its necessary scope, without claiming a complete formalization of the unquantified application.'),original=r'Previous studies (Tse & Viswanath, 2005) proved that given $N$ complex numbers, if each complex number follows a Gaussian distribution, then the linear summation of these $N$ complex numbers also follows a Gaussian distribution of complex numbers.'+'\n\n'+source('B.1')['original_proof_md'],proof='',kind='external_theorem',role='statement_scope_explanation',assessment='scope_under_review',leanrole='partial_component',symbols=['kernel-response','mean','variance','independence','som'])
 add('metrics','实验指标与频率集合定义','Experimental metrics and frequency-set definitions','Section5.1–5.2; C.10',r'p_{\rm low}=\frac{\sum_{[u,v]\in\Omega_{\rm low}}\mathbb E_c|H_{uv}^{(c)}|^2}{\sum_{u,v}\mathbb E_c|H_{uv}^{(c)}|^2}',[8,9,33,34],[('原能量比的总能量应非0；像素误差、平均重建误差及epoch数作为实验报告量。','The energy ratio needs nonzero total energy. Pixel errors, mean reconstruction error and epoch counts are experimental reporting quantities.')],[SOM],[st('保留实验规范','Retain experimental conventions',r'Ωlow是图像谱四角各八分之一范围；原可视化把低频移到中心，并为清晰修改DC展示强度。这个展示处理不是DFT恒等式，也不改变源数学定理。',r'Ω_low consists of the four corner ranges of one eighth of each axis. The visualizations move low frequencies to the center and adjust the displayed DC strength for clarity. This is a display convention, not a DFT identity and does not alter the mathematical theorem.')],('定义/实验规范入口，未构造不存在的指标证明目标。','A definition and experimental-convention entry; no nonexistent metric theorem is invented.'),original=r'We used the metric $$p_{\rm low}=\frac{\sum_{[u,v]\in\Omega_{\rm low}}\mathbb E_c[|H_{uv}^{(c)}|^2]}{\sum_{u,v}\mathbb E_c[|H_{uv}^{(c)}|^2]}$$ to measure the ratio of low-frequency components to all frequencies, where $\Omega_{\rm low}$ denoted the set of low-frequency components. Low-frequencies $[u,v]\in\Omega_{\rm low}$ were included in $u\in\{u|0\le u<M/8\}\cup\{u|7M/8\le u<M\}$ and $v\in\{v|0\le v<N/8\}\cup\{v|7N/8\le v<N\}$.'+'\n\n'+r'We used the metric $\Delta x_{mn}=\|[x^{*(1)}_{mn},x^{*(2)}_{mn},\ldots,x^{*(C)}_{mn}]-[\hat x^{(1)}_{mn},\hat x^{(2)}_{mn},\ldots,\hat x^{(C)}_{mn}]\|_2$ to measure the fitting error on the pixel $[m,n]$. Table 2 reports the number of epochs for the training of each model and its fitting error $\mathbb E_x[\|x-\hat x\|_2^2/N]$, where $N$ denoted the number of pixels in the image.',proof='',kind='definition',role='source_material',symbols=['low-frequency','som','input-spectrum','loss'])
 add('experiments','实验、结论与完整非证明页范围','Experiments, conclusion and all non-proof pages','Section5–6; AppendixC.1–C.10',[r'\mathrm{measured\ spectra,\ SOM,\ errors,\ correlations}'][0],[1,2,7,8,9,10,11,27,28,29,30,31,32,33,34],[],[SOM],[st('覆盖原实验而不提升范围','Cover experiments without enlarging the scope',r'正文和C.1–C.10覆盖训练epoch谱、zero/circular/mirror padding比较、深度/均值/核大小、upsampling重复、移频误差、相关统计与训练细节；参考文献和致谢页亦逐页登记。C.6/C.7及层位置的数学解释已独立列为目标，不藏在此条。',r'The main experiments and C.1–C.10 cover spectra across epochs, zero/circular/mirror padding, depth/mean/kernel size, upsampling repetition, shifted-frequency errors, correlations and training details. References and acknowledgements are also audited page by page. The mathematical interpretations in C.6/C.7 and layer placement have separate targets.'),st('保留作者明确的限制','Retain the authors’ explicit limitation',r'作者结论明确不是特定网络的确定性性质，且没有推max-pooling所以不扩到classification网络。实测含ReLU/BN等网络只能验证实验趋势，不能更改无activation精确命题的假设。',r'The conclusion explicitly excludes deterministic properties of a specific network and excludes classification networks because max pooling was not analyzed. Experiments containing ReLU or batch normalization support measured trends, without altering the assumptions of exact activation-free statements.')],('非证明经验入口；源数学推断已有独立目标，源图/表页和无证明页全部在inventory中可检索。','An empirical entry rather than a proof target. Mathematical inferences have separate targets; figure/table and non-proof pages are all searchable in the inventory.'),original=r'Results show that when the target frequency components were shifted by a smaller distance, it was more difficult to learn a decoder to fit the target image, i.e., yielding larger fitting errors in Figure 1(c.1,c.2). Besides, Figure 1(c.3) reports the average weight change $\|\Delta W\|$ over different DNNs, which was decreased along with the shifting distance.'+'\n\n'+r'Note that our findings can explain general trends of networks with above three operations, but cannot derive a deterministic property of a specific network, and cannot be extended to networks for image classification, because we have not derived the property of the max-pooling operation.',proof='',kind='empirical',role='source_material',symbols=['input-spectrum','som','depth','kernel-size','loss','pearson'])

