def add_issues(p):
 def issue(s,z,e,typ,pages,original,bz,be,impact,ie,related):
  ids=['decoder-'+r for r in related]
  id=p.issue('decoder-issue-'+s,z,e,typ,original,'formal PDF '+','.join(map(str,pages)),bz,be,impact,ie,ids)
  row=p.issues[-1];row['issue_type']=typ;row['source_refs']=[p.ref('formal',pages,'source issue '+s)]
  row['translations']['en'].pop('source_location',None)
  row['original_statement_status']='compound_clause_counterexample_verified' if typ=='statement_partial_counterexample' else 'counterexample_verified' if typ=='statement_counterexample' else 'scope_under_review'
  for r in p.rows:
   if r['id'] in ids:r['related_issue_ids'].append(id)
 issue('quotient-domain','原几何/R/χ/τ商的零分母','Zero denominators in the geometric/R/χ/τ quotients','definition_or_algorithm_boundary',[4,5,6,11,17,20,23],r'\sin(a\theta)/\sin\theta',r'θ=0或频率同坐标时，普通商0/0；χ完整和包含这些频率，不能排除必要项。有限和保留合法值n或K。',r'At θ=0 or equal-coordinate frequencies, the ordinary quotient is 0/0. The complete χ sum includes these frequencies, so they cannot be excluded. Finite sums retain legitimate values n or K.','全称商域问题；不否定有限DFT传播。','A universal quotient-domain issue, without refuting finite DFT propagation.',['geometric-sum','backpropagation','gaussian-response','zero-padding'])
